  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Thermal decomposition of ammonium dichromate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> on heating gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>HCl</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>KCl</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>MnCl</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub></math></p><p>The reaction of Aluminium with Sodium hydroxide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Al</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>)</mo></math> gives a salt and Hydrogen gas.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Al</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>On heating sodium nitrate it undergoes decomposition reaction and liberates oxygen and convert into sodium nitrite.</p></blockquote>"
